---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/atlas/Crumbs.astro';
import {articles} from '../../data/atlas/catalog';
import {root,articleUrl,orbitGuide,technologies} from '../../data/atlas/taxonomy';
import '../../styles/atlas.css';
const path=root+'orbits/',trail=[{name:'Satellite Applications Atlas',href:root},{name:'Compare satellite orbits',href:path}];
---
<BaseLayout title="Compare satellite orbits and technologies" description="Compare LEO, MEO and GEO for industrial satellite services. See how orbital geometry, sensors and the timing of a usable observation affect an operating decision." path={path} breadcrumbTrail={trail}><div class="atlas"><div class="atlas-simple-hero"><div class="shell"><Crumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},trail[0],{name:'Orbit guide'}]}/><h1>Compare satellite orbits</h1><p>Start with the measurement and its deadline. Altitude changes what a sensor can resolve, how long a satellite is in view and how far a signal must travel.</p></div></div>
 <section class="atlas-block"><div class="shell"><div class="atlas-heading-row"><h2>Three orbital choices</h2><a class="atlas-text-link" href="https://www.esa.int/articles/about-us/directorates/space-transportation/types-of-orbits">ESA orbit reference ↗</a></div><div class="atlas-orbit-guide">{orbitGuide.map((orbit,i)=><article><svg viewBox="0 0 120 65" aria-hidden="true" width="105" height="57"><circle cx="61" cy="35" r="10" fill="#6fc7bc"/><ellipse cx="61" cy="35" rx={[20,34,48][i]} ry={[14,19,24][i]} fill="none" stroke="#7aa9b3" stroke-width="1.5" transform="rotate(-14 61 35)"/><circle cx={[81,94,108][i]} cy={[30,27,24][i]} r="3" fill="#e6e8c8"/></svg><h3>{orbit.name}</h3><strong>{orbit.full}</strong><p class="atlas-label">{orbit.range}</p><p>{orbit.strength}</p><p>{orbit.trade}</p></article>)}</div><p class="atlas-fine">Orbit sketches are schematic. <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/catalog-of-earth-satellite-orbits/">NASA’s catalogue of Earth orbits ↗</a></p></div></section>
 <section id="technologies" class="atlas-block"><div class="shell atlas-split"><div class="atlas-section-intro"><h2>What the technology delivers</h2><p>A payload may measure the surface, transmit a message or supply a timing reference.</p></div><div class="atlas-tree">{technologies.map(([name,body])=><details><summary>{name}<span class="atlas-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="atlas-branch"><p>{body}</p></div></details>)}</div></div></section>
 <section class="atlas-block"><div class="shell"><h2>See the orbit decision in practice</h2><ul class="atlas-link-list">{articles.slice(0,3).map(a=><li><a href={articleUrl(a)+'#orbits'}>{a.title} →</a></li>)}</ul><a class="atlas-text-link" href={root}>Back to the Atlas →</a></div></section></div></BaseLayout>
